a moment of panic on a bustling Street  in South London police target a man  suspected of stabbing two people within  minutes he was shot dead armed officers  who were part of a proactive  counterterrorism surveillance operation  and were following the suspect on foot  were in immediate attendance and shot a  male suspect dead at the scene the  suspect had been recently released from  prison where he had been serving a  sentence for Islamist related terrorism  the suspect was wearing a hoax explosive  device this is the first such attack to  happen in a relatively unknown London  suburb and it's shaken the people here  incredibly shocked and absolutely  devastated that this should have  happened and that should happen here in  Stretton we pride ourselves on being an  enclosed inclusive welcoming community  and so many people from so many  different backgrounds living you know  very harmoniously together and it's a  place where you just wouldn't expect  this to happen I think it's it's you  know obviously that was like one street  away from where you live it makes you  feel a bit unsafe because you know if we  had left the house 10 minutes earlier we  would have been here as it was happening  rather than you know just as I had  finished you know it's it makes just  feel yeah not very very safe forensic  teams remain at the scene combing the  area for clues  politicians took to Twitter including  the British prime minister who extended  his sympathy to those affected and  London Mayor Sadiq Khan who said  terrorists seek to divide us and destroy  our way of life here in London we will  never let them succeed this is the  second terrorism related stabbing  incident in London in just over two  months and it's likely to put intense  pressure on Boris Johnson and his  government to do more to prevent such  attacks in the future stencil al Jazeera  London
 

